<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bolesław the Elder of Niemodlin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1362</span> · Also known as Bolesław I of Niemodlin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bolesław the Elder was a Silesian Piast duke, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolko-i-of-opole">Bolko I of Opole</a>. On his father's death in 1313 he received the castle town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niemodlin">Niemodlin</a>, west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/opole">Opole</a>, as a separate duchy. He was close to the Bohemian court and in 1327 did homage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>. His line held Niemodlin until it returned to Opole in 1382.</p></div>
